31. Ten-run stability and reliability metrics

Exactly ten runs remain required.

The shared repeated-iteration evaluator calculates:

runCount = 10

requirementStability[REQ_ID]:
  satisfied
  violated
  undetermined
  agreementRate

testStability[TEST_ID]:
  satisfied
  violated
  undetermined
  agreementRate

totalDistinctDefects
repeatedDefectCount
uniqueDefectCount
newDefectsByRun[RUN_ID]
unexplainedVarianceCount
requirementsWithCompleteAgreement
requirementsWithDisagreement

Historical or invalidated runs are excluded.
Wrong-iteration and wrong-candidate runs are excluded.

These metrics expose:
- unstable requirements;
- unstable tests;
- stochastic failure concentration;
- novel-defect discovery by run;
- unexplained variance.

They do not create new release thresholds unless existing convergence rules already require the corresponding condition.

Project-level operational metrics include:
- accepted external responses;
- rejected responses;
- stale responses;
- execution failures;
- downstream-discovered silent failures;
- defects caught before baseline;
- defects found after baseline;
- defects found during final verification;
- release reversals;
- artifact identity mismatches;
- regression recurrences;
- human correction frequency;
- native test executions;
- external test executions;
- blocked capabilities;
- evidence-insufficiency failures;
- independence violations.

Browser-local data cannot be represented as population-wide telemetry.

31.1 Closed metric universes

Every coverage, completion, agreement, stability, reliability, and zero-count metric publishes:
- metric identity and derivation version;
- the closed universe definition;
- numerator;
- denominator;
- exact included IDs;
- exact excluded IDs and reasons;
- current scope hash;
- evidence references;
- calculated value and disposition.

